Case 2: EXISTS / IN on an indexed outer, a derived table of few rows -> INNER JOIN with a DISTINCT derived table     

===================================================
count(*)    
9     

Query plan:
temp(distinct)
    subplan: hash-join (inner join)
                 edge:  term[?]
                 outer: sscan
                            class: tm node[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 inner: sscan
                            class: ta node[?]
                            cost:  ? card ?
                 cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
(select distinct tm.cb from tm tm, ta ta where tm.ca=ta.cb)
Query plan:
idx-join (inner join)
    outer: sscan
               class: av? node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: tb node[?]
               index: i_tb_ca term[?] (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select count(*) from tb tb inner join (select distinct tm.cb from tm tm, ta ta where tm.ca=ta.cb) av? (av_?) on av?.av_?=tb.ca
